.TH FATHOM_CMP 1  "fathom 0.1.0-alpha.1" 
.SH NAME
fathom\-cmp \- Compare any two episodes or revisions: the composed delta over a range (`e5.3`)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfathom cmp\fR [\fB\-\-root\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-save\fR] [\fB\-\-note\fR] [\fB\-\-list\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fISPEC\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Compare any two episodes or revisions: the composed delta over a range (`e5.3`)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<ROOT>\fR [default: .]
The repository to read
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the comparison as one JSON line on stdout (`fathom.compare/1`)
.TP
\fB\-\-save\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Keep this comparison under a name, so the next person says `since\-the\-refactor` instead of typing the endpoints
.TP
\fB\-\-note\fR \fI<NOTE>\fR
Why the name exists, kept with it
.TP
\fB\-\-list\fR
List the saved comparisons and exit
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fISPEC\fR]
The comparison: `HEAD~9..HEAD`, `77aa0c..e8f1a2`, `main@1a2b3c..feat/x@9f8e7d`, or a saved name
